# L §2.5 Keys: a bare key in a membership list takes the other operand's index; z is not a key of cat, so
# LOAD-KEY "<key> is not a key of <index>" (L §8.3), at load.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2027-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2027-12-31

index cat = [a, b, c, s]
def r[q in cat]: num at reader
  rule base = 1
  rule nil beats base = 0 when q in [c, z]

ask qb: r[q] for q in cat law 2026-12-31
=== expect
refused: LOAD-KEY z is not a key of cat ...
